$\begin{align}
4^4\cdot 4^3&=4^{4+3}
\\\\
&=4^{7}
\end{align}$

This follows from the general rule $x^m\cdot x^n=x^{m+n}$. Note that the powers have the same base.

We can also see this is correct by expanding the powers.

$\begin{align}
4^4\cdot 4^3&=\underbrace{4\cdot 4\cdot 4\cdot 4}_\text{4 times}\cdot\underbrace{4\cdot 4\cdot 4}_\text{3 times}
\\\\\\
&=\underbrace{4\cdot 4\cdot 4\cdot 4\cdot 4\cdot 4\cdot 4}_\text{7 times}
\\\\
&=4^{7}
\end{align}$
